1) When allowed to choose more than one option on summoning spells, the same option may be chosen more than once. For example, with a Summons III, two options are available. This means that if both options are used for the same thing: three first-level creatures could be summoned, or one third-level creature could be summoned, or one first-level creature could be summoned for four times as long.
2) Demons are assumed to be beings of another plane who are brought into the caster's plane through the use of an elemental force (one not of the Demon's plane). Thus, the Demon and caster do not make RRs during the summons. See Creatures & Monsters for a full description of Demons. If no type for a Demon is given, use the following table to determine a Demon's type. The GM may wish to this type system to account for the types of Demons he wishes to use in his world. Level Type 1-2 I 3-5 II 6-10 III 11-15 IV 16-20 V 21-40 VI 41+ Beyond the Pale CLERIC BASE LIST 2.4.6 SUMMONS
